# Who must approve a pull request that touches a path. GitHub enforces it once main's ruleset asks
# for a code owner's review (the releasing skill sets that up when the repository goes public).
#
# Everything is the maintainer's for now, named by their own account: an organization cannot be a
# code owner, only a person or one of its teams. The paths below are named again so that they stay
# with the maintainer when the first line is given to a wider team: they run by themselves, steer
# Claude, or ship to every application (CLAUDE.md, "Security", which also says how this list and
# permissions.ask in .claude/settings.json divide the work). A later line wins over an earlier one;
# a pattern without a leading slash matches at any depth.

*                       @Horomix

/.claude/               @Horomix
/.vscode/               @Horomix
/.mcp.json              @Horomix
CLAUDE.md               @Horomix
